[2026-09-27T12:16:40.913+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]   "summary": "REQ-1-1-1 is a leaf node (no children, execution-bearing scenarios), so it owns the full registration chain: UI form -> auth client -> Express auth routes -> auth service -> sqlite users/sessions, plus the shared global session state and the deterministic seeded account. Reused existing scaffolds rather than creating parallel ones: backend/src/database/{init_db,db_runtime,seed_db}.js, backend/src/app.js route mounting, frontend/src/api/index.ts axios client, and frontend/src/App.tsx routing. New cohesive modules were materialized as DESIGN-only skeletons: backend/src/services/auth_service.js (rule constants + visible field messages + service signatures), backend/src/routes/auth_routes.js (thin /api/auth router contract with response shapes), frontend/src/api/authClient.ts (typed HTTP boundary incl. AuthRequestError fieldErrors), frontend/src/features/auth/SessionContext.tsx (single global session source of truth with status/user/signIn/signOut/refresh), frontend/src/features/auth/useRegistrationForm.ts (input + per-field error state), frontend/src/features/auth/AuthTextField.tsx (labelled input with inline field message), and frontend/src/pages/RegisterPage.tsx (the exactly-one-of-each control contract). init_db.js was extended with idempotent users/sessions DDL so the chain has a real persistence target. The seeded account (alice-dev / alice.dev@example.test / Valid-password-123!) is recorded as a DB seed contract on the existing seed_db.js entrypoint (idempotent, email already verified, seeded through auth_service.ensureVerifiedAccount) and is intentionally left for the TDD stage to implement so multiple errors surface together and username/email survive rejection. All behavior bodies (validation aggregation, hashing, SQLite writes, cookie session handling, navigation) remain TODO for TestDrivenDeveloper.",
