[2026-09-27T12:16:41.166+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "specification": "Extend the existing seedDatabase() transaction (do not add one-off connection helpers) so that startup seeding guarantees a pre-existing account: username `alice-dev`, email `alice.dev@example.test`, password `Valid-password-123!`, email_verified = 1. Implement it by delegating to auth_service.ensureVerifiedAccount({ username, email, password }) inside the existing withTransaction callback so the row is created through the same hashing path as registration and is immediately sign-in capable; keep it idempotent (INSERT OR IGNORE / upsert on username_lower and email_lower) so repeated seeds and repeated resets converge to the same single row and never duplicate or overwrite a conflicting user-created account. No frontend constant, fallback array, or test-only endpoint may substitute for this path. The seed must run before E2E and through the normal backend startup path, and must be reachable through GET /api/auth/session and POST /api/auth/login.",
