[2026-09-27T12:26:20.183+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-2]   "summary": "REQ-1-1-2 is a leaf node (no children) and owns the executable sign-in slice, so it designs the full UI -> API -> FUNC -> DB chain and reuses the REQ-1-1-1 auth spine already present in the workspace. Evidence gathered: frontend/src/api/authClient.ts already declared SignInInput with an email-only field, frontend/src/features/auth/SessionContext.tsx exposed signIn()/status/user but no consumer, frontend/src/App.tsx had only the '/' route, backend/src/routes/auth_routes.js had a not-implemented /login handler, and backend/src/services/auth_service.js had the users+sessions schema and the alice-dev seed contract. Owned boundaries designed here: form-state hook useSignInForm (generic 'Invalid credentials' failure owned as a constant), SignInPage with the exact 'Username or email' / 'Password' / 'Sign in' controls, the shared AccountMenu (upper-right session representation) plus RequireAuth guard, an authenticated WorkspacePage with explicit empty organization/repository/work-item states, and the /signin + /workspace route wiring. Reused: REQ-1-1-1-UI-auth-text-field (labelled input + inline role=\"alert\" message), REQ-1-1-1-UI-session-context (global auth state, now consumed by the new chrome), REQ-1-1-1-API-auth-client and REQ-1-1-1-API-auth-routes (sign-in/session boundary updated to a username-or-email identifier), REQ-1-1-1-FUNC-auth-service plus REQ-1-1-1-DB-seed-default-account and REQ-1-1-1-DB-users-sessions-schema (session record carries unique id, account id and active status; the pre-existing alice-dev account is seeded through the normal startup path, not a test fixture). One small edit landed in authClient.ts renaming SignInInput.email to identifier so the client, page and API share one field name; no business logic, validation, hashing or session persistence was implemented. SessionProvider is imported in frontend/src/main.tsx but the tree still needs to wrap <App /> with it, and the credential rules/session lifecycle remain explicit TDD work.",
