[2026-09-27T12:26:20.410+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-2]       "specification": "Provides { status: 'loading' | 'authenticated' | 'unauthenticated', user: SessionUser | null, signIn, signOut, refresh }. signIn(input: SignInInput) calls authClient.signIn with the identifier field, publishes the returned user and flips status to 'authenticated' so chrome and protected routes update from this single store. On mount refresh() must call fetchCurrentUser(), tolerate a failed restore by falling back to 'unauthenticated', and never leave status at 'loading'; that reload path is what keeps the signed-in username visible after a refresh or a direct reopen of a protected page. On a rejected sign-in the state must remain 'unauthenticated' with user null. TODO(TDD): implement the mount effect (currently a placeholder `void refresh;`).",
