[2026-09-27T12:26:23.087+08:00] [TestGenerator][REQ-1-1-2] # leaf-test-layer-selection
[2026-09-27T12:26:23.087+08:00] [TestGenerator][REQ-1-1-2] 
[2026-09-27T12:26:23.087+08:00] [TestGenerator][REQ-1-1-2] Use this skill when generating tests for a node that owns executable behavior.
[2026-09-27T12:26:23.087+08:00] [TestGenerator][REQ-1-1-2] 
[2026-09-27T12:26:23.087+08:00] [TestGenerator][REQ-1-1-2] ## Instructions
[2026-09-27T12:26:23.087+08:00] [TestGenerator][REQ-1-1-2] 
[2026-09-27T12:26:23.087+08:00] [TestGenerator][REQ-1-1-2] 1. Choose only layers that match the current node's owned interfaces and scenarios.
[2026-09-27T12:26:23.087+08:00] [TestGenerator][REQ-1-1-2] 2. If the requirement declares scenarios, generate E2E tests for those scenarios. Scenario presence is a strong signal for E2E coverage.
[2026-09-27T12:26:23.087+08:00] [TestGenerator][REQ-1-1-2] 3. Use Unit tests for owned FUNC or DB contracts when direct logic or persistence behavior is present.
[2026-09-27T12:26:23.087+08:00] [TestGenerator][REQ-1-1-2] 4. Use Integration tests for API, boundary wiring, and service collaboration.
[2026-09-27T12:26:23.087+08:00] [TestGenerator][REQ-1-1-2] 5. Use E2E tests for every current-node user-visible scenario flow; do not reduce scenario coverage to a simple render smoke test.
[2026-09-27T12:26:23.087+08:00] [TestGenerator][REQ-1-1-2] 6. Prefer one stable file per layer unless scenarios naturally split into coherent groups.
[2026-09-27T12:26:23.087+08:00] [TestGenerator][REQ-1-1-2] 7. Do not create tests for parent-owned shell behavior or child-owned future behavior.
[2026-09-27T12:26:23.087+08:00] [TestGenerator][REQ-1-1-2] 8. Before writing tests, translate every declared scenario into a private checklist: GIVEN is setup, WHEN is action, THEN is assertion. The generated test must follow that checklist without reversing any condition.
[2026-09-27T12:26:23.087+08:00] [TestGenerator][REQ-1-1-2] 9. Never assert the opposite of a requirement precondition. If the scenario says global navigation is visible, do not assert the logo/nav is absent. If it says a user can click a control, do not start by asserting the control is missing.
